erence rows are shown, never ranked, and do not shape the common sample.", "Persistence = the URMA analysis at the same hour of day from the newest analysis already issued at the start (URMA appears about 6 h after its valid time): a 24 h forecast uses the analysis of 24 h before the start, a 6 h forecast that of 18 h before. An analysis-based reference, not an operational forecast product. Reference rows are shown, never ranked, and do not shape the common sample."], "policy": "Rows whose start is not available in real time (ERA5, which assimilates observations from after the start, or IFS starts with same-day OISST sea temperature / ERA5 clouds) are shown as an unranked reference; ranked rows share one sample; group_rank = rank within single runs / ensemble means / post-processed products", "group_labels": {"single": "single runs (raw)", "ensmean": "ensemble means (raw)", "postproc": "post-processed on observations", "reference": "reference: start not available in real time (ERA5, or same-day OISST / ERA5 clouds; unranked)"}, "ci_block_sensitivity": {"block_starts": [1, 2, 4, 8], "median_ci_width": [0.264, 0.342, 0.398, 0.368], "rank_range": {"ifs": [[7, 8], [7, 8], [7, 8], [7, 9]], "gfs": [[11, 12], [11, 12], [11, 12], [11, 12]], "nbm": [[3, 5], [3, 5], [3, 5], [3, 5]], "aifs": [[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]], "aigfs": [[7, 8], [7, 8], [7, 8], [7, 8]], "raint": [[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]], "graphcast_ifs": [[4, 5], [4, 5], [4, 5], [4, 6]], "fuxi_ifs": [[3, 5], [3, 5], [3, 5], [3, 5]], "graphcast": [[9, 10], [9, 10], [9, 10], [9, 10]], "fuxi": [[6, 6], [6, 6], [5, 6], [5, 6]], "ukmo": [[9, 10], [9, 10], [9, 10], [9, 10]], "wrf": [[13, 14], [13, 14], [13, 14], [13, 14]], "mpas": [[13, 14], [13, 14], [13, 14], [13, 14]], "icon": [[11, 12], [11, 12], [11, 12], [11, 12]], "cesm": [[15, 15], [15, 15], [15, 15], [15, 15]], "e3sm": [[16, 16], [16, 16], [16, 16], [16, 16]]}, "p_top": {"ifs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "gfs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "nbm": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "aifs": [0.034, 0.059, 0.061, 0.033], "aigfs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "raint": [0.966, 0.941, 0.939, 0.967], "graphcast_ifs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "fuxi_ifs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "graphcast": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "fuxi": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "ukmo": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "wrf": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "mpas": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "icon": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "cesm": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "e3sm": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}}, "rank_metric": "rmse", "corrected_method": "same correction for all: every model, rainfallAI included, gets the same additive correction fitted against the same station observations: a bias per lead day plus a bias per station and valid hour (00/06/12/18 UTC), the station terms shrunk toward zero (sum / (n + 20)); fitted leave-one-month-out (July, August, September, October starts), so no month is corrected with its own data. Only models scored on the common sample are corrected. This is a retrospective cross-validation sensitivity, not a calibration a forecaster could have run: the other months include later ones, and it does not undo each model's own earlier training or tuning.", "deg1_method": "1 deg smoothing view (sensitivity, not identical grid cells): every model field is averaged over a 1 x 1 deg box centred on each grid point of the model's own grid before it is interpolated to the stations; models with a native grid of 1 deg or coarser (CESM, E3SM) are unchanged. Temperature is height-adjusted from a common terrain dataset averaged the same way, not from each model's own orography.", "ci_method": "95 % intervals from a moving-block bootstrap over the 38 start dates: 1,000 resamples (fixed seed), each made of blocks of 4 consecutive starts (12 days; neighbouring starts overlap in time and share weather), each start kept whole (its full map or station set and all 7 lead days); the RMSE over all lead days (from the summed squared errors) is recomputed in every resample on the same common sample. rank_range = 2.5-97.5 % range of a model's rank among the ranked models, p_top = share of resamples in which it ranks first. The 'same correction for all' values are reused in the resamples, not refitted. The block length is a choice: fair.ci_block_sensitivity repeats the as-run intervals and rank ranges with blocks of 1, 2, 4 and 8 starts.", "ci_resamples": 1000, "ci_seed": 20261109, "deg1_common_cases": 2414146}}